each whose body copies a field the element may omit: each element of the
target list needs a value, and a copy body has no fallback.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: close({
	u!: [...close({id?: string})]
})
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: close({
	u!: [...string]
})

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		u: _each(v0_0.u, _item.id)
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: close({u!: [...string]})
-- out/error --
error[E0343]: u[].id is optional in 0.0, and each element of 1.0's u needs a value
 --> history/1.0.thema:8:20
  |
8 |         u: _each(v0_0.u, _item.id)
  |                          ^^^^^
  |
  = note: an _each whose body copies a field writes one element per source element, so the field must be present in every one
